// BUGS #37, the instance that was live in the tree. `Map` has no `delete` — there
// is no `__map_delete` in src/runtime/runtime.sf at all — and a Map receiver is
// classified as a builtin, so the "no such method" check above the fall-through
// skipped it and the call was silently dropped.
//
// pantry/src/commands/remove.sf did exactly this. `pantry remove <pkg>` compiled
// clean, emitted zero `__map_*` instructions for the delete, and removed nothing.
// Two files in the tree were affected and no test covered either.
var m: Map<String, Int> = {"a": 1}
m.delete("a")
IO.println("unreachable")
